+## L15: Antigravity child model notice
+
+### Facts
+
+- The notice is `AGY-NATIVE-CHILD-MODEL-NOTICE`, surfaced as the diagnostic `agy-native-child-model-mismatch` (`PC/hooks/antigravity-pretool-guard.mjs:668-669`). It is computed in `evaluateNativeChildCall` (`PC/lib/agy-native-goldfish.mjs:112-141`).
+- **Mapping.** `expected` is the registry cell of the child's duty: `goldfish-implementor` is `duty.implement`, `goldfish-deep` is `duty.deep`, `goldfish-mechanic` is `duty.mechanic` (:39, :98-104). The consumer's expected value `gemini-3.8-flash-medium` is the implementor cell (`pipeline.user.yaml:178`). `resolved` is the child's hook payload `modelName` (:130).
+- **Status.** `match` on equal normalized names, `tier-match` when both are the same `flash`, `flash-lite` or `pro` family, else `mismatch` (:133-134). `tierOf` knows only those three families, so `gemini-4-hydrogen-tiered-high` has no tier and is always a mismatch against a flash cell. Only a mismatch earns the notice (:136-140); it never denies (G20-43).
+- **Scope.** The check runs for the three code-writer roles only (:125); a Critic child returns before it. The Critic inherits by design and is never noticed.
+- **Which duties may be `inherit`.** The dispatch guard admits `inherit` or no Model only for a duty whose every Antigravity route `nativeTier` is `inherit` (`PC/lib/dispatch-model-enforcement.mjs:187-199`). The tier table gives `inherit` to `duty.critic_normal` and `duty.critic_high_risk` only; `duty.implement`, `duty.mechanic` and `duty.deep` are `flash` (`PC/lib/model-role-route-source.mjs:37-49`).
+- **Is it wrong for `inherit`?** No, for a Goldfish: the measured fact is that a child launched without a Model, or with `inherit`, runs on the session model (reference `antigravity-native-dispatch.md:45-51`), so the notice reports a true difference between the registry cell and the model the child ran on. It is not wrong; it is unhelpful: its text names no repair (:139).
+- **Open contradiction (NOT resolvable by reading).** Because the Goldfish tiers are `flash`, the dispatch guard refuses `inherit` and an omitted Model for a Goldfish with `DISPATCH-MODEL-MISSING` before the child exists (`dispatch-model-enforcement.mjs:200-205`), and the reference says Goldfish roles pass `Model: "flash"` (:26-29). If the consumer's call really passed `inherit`, that guard did not run or did not apply; if it passed `flash`, the host now resolves the alias to the session model (the reference records `flash` resolving to `gemini-3.8-flash-tiered`, :46, which would have been `tier-match`). Which one happened is NOT MEASURED. Also, the generated Antigravity next step names no `Model` at all (`prepare-dispatch.mjs:120`): that gap is lane L10b and is not duplicated here.
+- Config note, not traced: `PC/config/runner-mappings.json:47` names `gemini-3.8-flash-high` for `implement` while `pipeline.user.yaml:178` names flash-medium; which source the notice reads (`registeredFunctionalTaskRoutes`) was not followed.
+
+### Smallest build (text only)
+
+Extend the notice sentence (:139) with the two named repairs: "If the parent call passed `inherit` or no Model, re-issue it with `Model: "flash"` (the dispatch guard requires it for this role); if it passed `flash`, the host resolved the alias to the session model: nothing to repair, the observation is recorded in the verdict `modelCheck`." No change of the check, the families or the verdict shape.
